# Renault Megane IV five-door hatchback, 2016-2022.
#
# The fourth-generation Megane in its phase-1 form (2016-2020), on sale in
# Britain from the summer of 2016 and withdrawn in July 2022, when Renault UK
# replaced the combustion Megane with the electric Megane E-Tech. The British
# range had the hatch and the Sport Tourer estate only; the saloon was never
# sold here.
# https://www.autocar.co.uk/ (18 July 2022, cited in the reference pack)
#
# Dimensions 4.359 x 1.814 x 1.445 m, wheelbase 2.669 m. Source: the reference
# pack's notes. The hull measures 4.359 m on a 2.669 m wheelbase (61.2 per
# cent) and 1.814 m wide; mirrors take it to 1.910 m.
#
# The car photographed is a **GT**, with its deeper front bumper and larger
# alloys, and the GT is what is modelled. Shape reference: a near-side view
# taken about 10-15 degrees aft of the side axis with the rear lamp edge and
# tailgate lip visible, a front three-quarter and a rear three-quarter. A true
# elevation was rendered for coherence. All glazing panes stand 10-18 mm clear
# of the local body surface.
#
# Colours are from the Renault UK brochure of 1 October 2016, evidence grade
# (a): Glacier White (solid); Arctic White, Mercury, Dune, Diamond Black,
# Titanium Grey, Cosmos Blue and Steel Blue (metallic); Flame Red and Iron Blue
# (Renault i.d. metallic). Four are modelled: Glacier White, Mercury, Diamond
# Black and Flame Red. Weights white 3, grey 3, black 2, red 2, total 10,
# provisional pending the central rebase.
#
# Speed 195 km/h, the GT's quoted maximum. Comfort 110/495, on the line
# 330 + 1.5 x 110: a quiet, well-damped family hatchback. Classes 0,1.
#
# Dates are road presence: July 2016 intro, retires staggered 2030-2033 on a
# fourteen- to seventeen-year tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/renault-megane-iv.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/renault-megane-iv.dae (113 objects). References:
# citycars/references/renault-megane-iv/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the headlamp treatment is more angular than the
# photographs and the rear bumper flatter. At 128 px the low wide body, the
# swept lamps and the pronounced hatch spoiler read as the Megane IV.

obj=citycar
